# Environment variables — Astro / Cloudflare Workers rewrite
# ============================================================
#
# Nothing here is wired up yet (Phase 2+ of the migration — D1, auth, and the
# Cron Trigger haven't been built). This file documents the *planned* shape so
# agents and contributors have something concrete to check env names/shapes
# against instead of ever opening a real `.env`/`.env.local` file.
#
# Do not commit `.env` or `.env.local`. Astro loads `.env`/`.env.local`
# automatically in dev; real values in production/CI go in the Cloudflare
# dashboard (`wrangler secret put <NAME>`) or GitHub Actions secrets — never
# in a committed file.
#
# Differences from the old Next.js app's root .env.example, see the plan doc:
#   - DATABASE_URL / POSTGRES_URL_TEST are gone — D1 is a Cloudflare binding
#     (wrangler.jsonc), not a connection string.
#   - CRON_SECRET is gone — the sync job becomes a native Cloudflare Cron
#     Trigger, not a publicly reachable HTTP endpoint.
#   - NEXT_PUBLIC_* becomes Astro's PUBLIC_* convention.

# WCA OAuth
CLIENT_ID="your-wca-client-id"
CLIENT_SECRET="your-wca-client-secret"

# Application URL (OAuth redirects)
# Development: http://localhost:4321
# Production: https://www.cubingkerala.org
PUBLIC_BASE_URL="http://localhost:4321"

# WhatsApp
PUBLIC_WHATSAPP_CONTACT_URL="https://wa.me/cubingkerala_cofounder_number"

# Admin (server-only — never prefix with PUBLIC_)
# WCA website user id and/or WCA ID of the account that can open /requests
ADMIN_USER_ID="your-wca-numeric-user-id"
ADMIN_WCA_ID="YYYYXXXX99"
